# Password Cracking with John the Ripper (JtR)

## Overview
This project demonstrates practical password auditing using **John the Ripper (JtR)**, a powerful open-source password cracking tool.  
The exercise highlights the importance of strong password policies and provides hands-on experience in ethical password security testing.

---

## Objectives
- Learn the basics of password cracking using JtR.
- Understand different cracking modes (dictionary, brute-force, incremental).
- Showcase security implications of weak password practices.
- Document ethical guidelines for responsible use.

---

## Tools & Environment
- **Tool:** John the Ripper (community-enhanced version, `jumbo` build)
- **Environment:** Linux (Kali preferred) or macOS
- **Files:** Sample password hashes (non-production test data only)

